🤝 5. Freedom World should support creators even when they leave

This is what makes your vision different from simply creating a game marketplace.

Imagine a group of four developers who meet through Freedom World.

They build their first game together. Later, they establish an independent studio and release three more games.

They can continue their careers, develop new intellectual property, and pursue other commercial relationships without being restricted merely because they got their start here.

Their original Freedom World game can remain on the platform under its agreed license.

They can return for annual competitions, mentor newcomers, showcase their latest work, or collaborate on another Freedom World project.

Their independence doesn’t have to mean the end of their relationship with the community.

We want creators to stay because they find value in Freedom World, not because they’re unable to leave.

